22. Powers and functions of the Board of Governors. {l)The Boarrl ofGovernors shall have the power of general supervision over the Institute and s:rallhold the Vice-Chancellor and the Authorities accountable for all the, functionr; ofthe Institute. The Board of Governors shall have all powers of the lnstitute notexpressly vested in an Authority or officer by this Act and all other -powers notexpressly mentioned by this Act that are necessary for the performance of itsfunclions.
(2) Without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing powers, the Boar<l ofGovernors shall have the following powers: -
(a) to approve the proposed annual plaq of work, the annual and revisedbudgets, the annual report and the annual statement ofaccount; -
(b) to hold, control and lay down policy for the administration of the property,funds and investments of the Institute, including the approval of the sale rrndpurchase or acquisition of imrnovable . property;
(c) to oversee the quality and relevance of the Institute's acidernicprogrammers and to review the academic affairs;
(d) to approve the appointment ofthe Deans, Professors, Associate professorsand such other senior faculty and senior administrators as may be prescribed;
(e) to institute schemes, directions and guidelines for the tems and conditionsof appointment of all, officers, teachers and other employees of the Institute;
(f)(g)
to approve strategic pians;
to approve financial resource development plans of the Institute;
(h) to consider the drafts of Statutes and Regulations proposed by 1heSyndicate and the Academic Council and deal with them in the manner ixprovided for in sections 3l and 32, as the case rnay be:Provided that the Board of Governors may frarne a statute or Regulation on itsinitiative and approve it after calling for the advice of the Syndicate-or .-heAcademic Council as the case may be;
(i) to annul by order in writing the- proceedings of any Authority or officer, ifthe Board of Governors is satisfied that such'prodeedings are not in accordancewith the provisions of this Act, statutes or Regulations-after 'calling upon stchAuthority or officer show cause why such proceedings should not ue ainutteo;
q) to recommend to the chancellor removal of any member of the Board ofCovernors in accordance with the provisions of this ActiDot'/'-,'

