25. Powers and of the Syndicate,{l) The Syndicate shall be theexecutive body of the Institute and shall, subject to the provisions of this Act "andthe Statutes, exercise general supervision ovei the affairs and management of theInstitute.
(2) Without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing powers, andsubject to the provisions of this Act,, the statutes and directions of the Board ofGovernors the Syndicate shall have the following powers: -
(a) to consider the annual report, the annual and revised budgetestimates and to submit these to the Board of Govemors;(b) to transfer and accept transfer of movable properfy on behalf ofthe Instilute;
(c) to enter into, vary, carry out and cancel contracts on behalfoftheInstitute;
(d) to cause proper books of account to be, kept for all sums of moneyreceived and expended by the 'Institute and for the.assets andliabilities of the Institute;
(e) to inv,est any money belonging to the Institute including anyunapplied income in any of the securities described in section 2bof the Trusts Act, 1882 (Act I1 of 1882), or in the purchase ofiryryoyabfe property or in such other manner, as it miy prescribe,with the like power of varying such investments;(0 to receive and manage any propefiy transferred, and grants,bequests, trust, gifts, donations, endorvments, and othercontributions made to the Institute;
(g) to administer any funds placed at the disposal of the Institute forspecified purposcs;(h) to provide the buildings, libraries, premises, furnitwe, apparatus,equipment and other means required for calying out the ivork ofthe Inst itute;(i)to establish and maintain halls of residence and hosters or approve. orlicense hostels or lodgings for the residence ofstudents;
to recornmend to the Board of Governors admission of educationalinstitutions to the privileges of the Institute and withdraw suchprivileges;
0)

endstream
endobj
