26. Academic Council. -(l) There shall be an Academic Council of theInstitute consisting of the following. -
(a) the Vice Chancellor who shall be its Chairperson;
(b) the Pro Vice-Chancellor (Admin & Finance);
(c) the Pro Vice Chancellor (Academic & Research);
(d)prescribed;
the Deans of Faculties and such Heads of departments as may be
(e) five members representing the departments, institutes, ' and theconstituent schools to be elected in the manner prescribed by the Board ofGovernors;
(D five Professors including Emeritus Professors:
(g) the Registrar;
(h) the Director (QEC);
(i) The Director (ORIC);
CI) the Controller of Exarninations; and
(k) the Librarian.
(2) The Board of Governors shall appoint the members of the AcadernicCouncil, other than the ex-officio and the elected members, on the recommendationof the Vice Chancellor:
Provided that as regards the five professors and the members representing thedepartments, institutes and the constituent schools the Board of Governors may, asan alternative to elections, prescribe, a procedure for proposal ofa panel of namesby the Representation Committee set up in terms of section 28. Appointment ofpersons proposed by the Representation Committee may be rnade by the board ofGovernors on the recommendation of the Vice Chancellor.
(3) Members-of the Academic Council phall hold office for three years.(4) The Academic Council shall meet at least once in each quarter.(5) The quorum for meetings of the Academic Council shall be. onehalf of the total number of members, a fraction being counted as one.

endstream
endobj
