Statement of Obiects and Reasoru
The maior hindrance in Pakistan padicularly in remote areas are access tohigher education followed by low pass percentage of undergraduate students. Theirdesire to get Higher Education often does not meet reality because of limited or noaccess to quality higher educational institutions. The existing universities cannotcater to the growing demand of the students seeking admission for M. Phil and PhDin the higher education Institutions.
Presently, in Sahiwal there is no private university or institute availablewhich can cater the demand of the students for higher education purposes in betweenf-ahore, Multan, Bahawalpur and Faisalabad for quality e.ducation. To access qualityhigher education students, have to bear too much transportation and hostel cost,
C.h'fa4;Y ht^-"^d
Ravi Institute(Rl), Sahiwal is located at 6 KM Pakpattan Road which easilycpnnects this Institute crmpus with Pakpattan, Okara and Bahawalnagar district, ThisInstitute will have very positive developmental effects within the areas of SouthemPunjab. The catchment areas of this Institute will extend to almost five distric8 ofPunjab i.e. Sahiwal, Pakpattan, Okara, Vehari and Khanewal. It will be coveringpopulation of 30 Million approximately.
